TEST 10624 -- OSPF  Silicon tables synced.
===========================================================================
Run:    2026-10-01 08:27-08:49 NZDT, tb470, bench-runner (queue CAMPAIGN-QUEUE-2026-09-29.md
        row 12, sentinel device-testing-67). Hand-driven: no framework script.
Build:  awplus_main-20260923-20 (stack and IE520-sa)
DUT:    IE520 3-member VCStack "IE520-stk" (members 1/3/4, master member 3), router MAC
        0000.cd37.0d6f. OSPF neighbour and route source: the standalone IE520-sa
        (84e3.2787.0780), standing in for the case's Ixia OSPF interface.
Case:   AWPTCM-T10624 (ck.db), objective "OSPF Routes correctly added to silicon.". One step:
        "Test routes in silicone and IP Route table correctly updated with fluctuating OSPF
        routes. start ixia ospf protocol interface with 500 routes / Wait until OSPF neighbour
        get into FULL state / Show IP route / Show platform table IP / Setup IP Stream via
        advertised route at 95% of wirespeed" -> expected "Check both output displays the 500
        routes correctly / Expect wirespeed routing of packets via OSPF route."
        Emulation: the SA advertises 500 routes into OSPF (500 static /24s, `redistribute
        static`), so they arrive at the DUT as O E2 routes. An Ixia would more often inject them
        as its own LSAs. "Fluctuating" is done by withdrawing and re-adding routes at the SA.

VERDICT: PASS.
  OSPF neighbour Full. The DUT's IP route table AND the silicon table (`show platform table
  ip`, every stack member) each held exactly the 500 advertised routes, and tracked every
  fluctuation:
    500 -> 0 (redistribution off) -> 500 (on) -> 400 (100 withdrawn) -> 500 (re-added),
  RIB, FIB and silicon agreeing on every member at every read.
  Traffic via the advertised routes at 95 % of wirespeed (1514 B, 77,210 pps, 935 Mbps):
    30 s: 2,316,301 / 2,316,301 delivered (100.0000 %), all 500 destination prefixes reached.
  The data plane followed each table state: 0 % with the routes withdrawn, 100 % with 500,
  80.0026 % with 400 (the 100 withdrawn prefixes, and only those, not received), 100 % after
  the re-add.
  Controls: with no OSPF, 0 of 772,101. Received frames TTL 62 (routed by the DUT and the SA).

